+# Final report: Track A (Chirantan)
+
+Name: Chirantan. Track: A (Today, Engine, Book including Risk & Finance, Munim, hardcoded-versus-real). Branch: `fix/ch-trackA` in `C:\ripple`, cut from `main` `4a8d820b`.
+Branch state: **nothing committed or pushed**. The fixes are in the working tree and in `docs/audit/chirantan/trackA.patch`. `main`, `bugbounty` and `redundant` do not contain them yet.
+
+1. **Frontend routes discovered and tested.** 9 routes exist (`/login`, `/setup`, `/app/today`, `/app/engine`, `/app/book`, `/app/khata`, `/app/orders`, `/app/inventory`, `/app/settings`). Track A tested 3 of them as **12 route states**: Today; Engine as Network, Flow, Decisions, Table; Book as Position, Risk & Finance, Ledger (Today and Book also at 390 px).
+2. **Controls.** 527 control observations: 405 at 1440 px and 122 at 390 px. **PASS 497, PASS (explained) 2, FAIL 0, BLOCKED 0, NOT APPLICABLE 28.** The two explained passes are the "Export CSV" download link, which the sweep reports as a failed request because a download aborts the navigation; the file download was verified separately (195 lines). Not applicable means disabled or hidden in that state (for example the phone layout hides desktop navigation). Plus 34 user-journey checks, all PASS.
+3. **Backend endpoints.** 86 route definitions found in the source: 76 mounted (29 GET, 32 POST, 4 PUT, 7 PATCH, 4 DELETE, including `/api/health`, `/health` and the web-app catch-all) and 10 not mounted. 24 mounted routes are exercised by the Track A Postman collection. The rest belong to Tracks B and C.
+4. **Postman MCP.** Not available in this session; no Postman tools were exposed. No remote workspace or collection was inspected.
+5. **Postman CLI.** Not installed (`postman` not found). **Newman** (Postman's open-source runner) was used instead, installed outside the repository. Local only; no Postman authentication was involved.
+6. **Collection.** `postman/collections/ripple-api.json` (generated by `postman/build_collection.py`), plus `postman/environments/local.example.json` (no secrets). 68 requests in 8 folders. Final run: **61 requests executed, 7 skipped** (the supervisor folder, which needs a password supplied at run time); the supervisor folder run separately: 9 requests.
+7. **Assertions.** Final owner run: **110 passed, 0 failed.** Supervisor run: **14 passed, 0 failed.** The first run had 1 failure, in the collection itself (the supervisor skip logic); fixed and rerun.
+8. **Browser errors and unexpected text.** None on any route load or control click (no console error or warning, page error, failed asset, HTTP error, `undefined`, `NaN`, `[object Object]`, stack trace). Defects found by other means: a blank app after a malformed response (A-004), raw error identifiers on screen (A-011), the same runway text for unrelated questions (A-001), a stray `₹-` in a sentence (A-005).
+9. **Authentication and authorisation.** Not signed in: 401 on today, engine, guard, book and Munim; a write without the `X-Ripple` header gets 403 before anything else. Supervisor: 403 on today, engine, guard, book and "log a miss"; Munim returns no money tool for them. **A-003 (High):** the login, demo and AI rate limits could be bypassed with a forged `X-Forwarded-For` header (unlimited password guesses). Fixed in code, with a per-account limit added. Cross-business reads were checked only for Munim's tools (arguments cannot point a tool at another business); the full matrix is Track C's.
+10. **Security findings by severity.** Critical: none. High: A-003 (fixed in code, deployment check open), A-006 (a branch commits `node_modules`, `dist` and a SQLite database; open, not on `main`). Medium: A-007 (about 1,700 lines of never-mounted backend, including a `/demo/reset` route; open). Low: A-009 (demo-creation limits could lock out people on one network address). Info: A-010 (11 unused routes).
+11. **AI, chatbot and speech-to-text.** A-001 (the fallback answered nearly everything with the runway text; fixed, with two new tools for receivables and the Risk and Finance engine) and A-002 (blank question accepted; fixed). With a stub provider: a provider exception, an empty reply and an invented number all fall back to a labelled template answer; tools cannot be redirected to another business; a supervisor cannot call a finance tool. Input limits all refused correctly. Microphone permission denied shows a clear message with Dismiss. **Not tested:** a live model, prompt injection against a live model, real recording and playback, AI answers in the 7 languages without a template. Tamil and Hindi help text is English (no reviewed translation).
+12. **Financial engine and database integrity.** The engine agrees with independent arithmetic in 8 of 8 checks (a new payment lowers net by exactly its amount from its day; an extension raises net by the bill between the old and new due day; a later receipt lowers net in between; a split payment leaves half unpaid until the second half is due; safe-to-spend equals the lowest net minus the buffer; a payment-check option equals the baseline minus the payment). Two sandboxes with the same books produce identical runs; the risk figures repeat for the same run. The Books check passes 8 of 8 on the demo. A-005: server-written money text lost paise and could print `₹-`; fixed. Not tested here: migrations, concurrency, transaction rollback (Track C).
+13. **Bugs fixed and files changed.** Fixed: A-001, A-002, A-003 (code), A-004, A-005, A-008, A-011, A-012. 13 files modified, plus new files (`ErrorBoundary.tsx`, four test files, two Playwright scripts, the Postman files and this audit folder); see `trackA.patch`. Modified: `backend/app/core/auth.py`, `backend/app/api/auth_routes.py`, `backend/app/api/app_routes.py`, `backend/app/services/munim.py`, `backend/app/services/fixes.py`, `backend/app/services/guard.py`, `frontend/src/App.tsx`, `frontend/src/pages/Login.tsx`, `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`, `.env.example`, `README.md`, and two test-helper timeouts.
+14. **Regression tests added and results.** Backend `unittest`: 31 new (15 in `test_trackA_fixes.py`, 8 in `test_trackA_recompute.py`, 8 in `test_trackA_munim_provider.py`) , all pass. Frontend `vitest`: 27 new (`errorCodes.test.ts`), all pass. Playwright: 34 journey checks (`e2e/regression-trackA.mjs`), all pass; before the fix the crash-recovery checks failed. Postman: the collection above.
+15. **Build and type-check (actual).** `npx tsc -b`: 0 errors. `npx vitest run`: 85 passed. `npm run build`: built. `python -m unittest discover`: **158 tests OK, 1 skipped**. One earlier run of the 158 had 1 failure, a 60-second wait for the risk run that timed out while the machine was saturated by browser sweeps; the waits are now 180 seconds and two later runs passed.
+16. **Unresolved defects and impact.** A-003 deployment: on the real host set `TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS` and review `--forwarded-allow-ips='*'` in the `Dockerfile`; until then a direct client can still forge a single header. A-006: do not merge `multilingual-speech-to-text` as it is; check what `data/ripple.db` holds. A-007: delete or integrate the unmounted backend. A-009: check the proxy chain on the deployed site. A-010: decide on 7 undocumented, unused routes. The 7 requests that need a supervisor password are not in the default run.
+17. **Blocked or untested.** Postman MCP and CLI; a live AI model; real microphone and speaker; Firefox and Safari; the deployed site, HTTPS behaviour and Docker build; Engine at 390 px (a sweep was started and stopped because it took too long); widths between 390 and 1440; the other tracks' screens and endpoints.
+18. **Release-readiness recommendation (Track A scope).** The Track A screens and endpoints are fit for the demo and for peer testing. Before a public deployment: verify A-003 on the real proxy chain, resolve A-006 and A-007, and have Track C's authorisation matrix and secret scan come back clean. No Critical or High finding is open on the Track A screens themselves. This is evidence of what was tested, not proof that no defect remains.
+
+## Decisions I need from you
+
+1. A-003: which proxy sits in front of the deployed app, and how many? (sets `TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS`)
+2. A-007: delete the unmounted backend, or integrate it?
+3. A-006: may John's branch be cleaned (source files only) before anything is merged?
+4. Do you want the 7 unused routes (A-010) kept and documented, or removed?
+5. The fix terms (2% discount, 90% advance, 1.5% fee, 10 days) are invented assumptions that drive the "ways to fix" numbers. Make them settings and label them (see `hardcoded-vs-real.md`), or leave as they are for the demo?
